index 000000000..7673c41b1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/image-build-manifest-99ad22b32ba0b6ac.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+---
+features:
+  - |
+    When Kolla Ansible runs from a containerised deployer image which
+    carries a build manifest, ``/etc/kolla-ansible/manifest.json``, every
+    image the manifest names is pulled by digest rather than by tag, as
+    long as its tag is the build's. The manifest is a JSON object with a
+    ``format_version`` of 1, the ``tag`` the images were pushed with, and
+    ``images``, mapping each image's repository within
+    ``docker_namespace`` (its name, with any ``docker_image_name_prefix``)
+    to its ``sha256:`` digest. A deployment then runs exactly the images the
+    deployer was built with, even if their tag has since been pushed again.
+    Every ``<service>_image_full`` variable now resolves through the new
+    ``kolla_image_full`` lookup plugin, so a service whose ``<service>_tag``
+    is overridden, an image outside ``docker_registry`` and
+    ``docker_namespace``, and an image the manifest does not name are still
+    pulled by tag. The manifest's location is ``kolla_image_manifest_path``.
+  - |
+    A deployer image without a build manifest warns once and pulls every
+    image by tag, as before. Kolla Ansible installed with ``pip`` has no
+    manifest and is silent. A manifest built with a tag other than the
+    deployer's is refused, unless ``--override-deployer-checks`` is given.
+upgrade:
+  - |
+    Switching a deployment between images given by tag and by digest
+    changes every container's image reference, so every container is
+    recreated once, including MariaDB and RabbitMQ. This happens the first
+    time a deployer image with a build manifest deploys or upgrades a
+    deployment last deployed by tag, and again if a later deployer has no
+    manifest. Do it during an upgrade, which restarts every container
+    anyway.
+  - |
+    A build manifest which cannot be read, or whose ``format_version`` this
+    Kolla Ansible does not understand, is an error rather than a reason to
+    pull by tag, and ``--override-deployer-checks`` does not change that.
+    To pull every image by tag regardless, set ``kolla_image_manifest_path``
+    to a path which does not exist.
+issues:
+  - |
+    With Docker's classic image store, ``prune-images`` removes images
+    pulled only by digest that no container uses, so run ``pull`` after
+    pruning, not before.
